// Airbnb and holiday let cleaning — its own Level-A item in the service band
// (navigation.ts), moved 25 Sep 2026 from /house-cleaning/airbnb-cleaning/ at
// the client's request, with no redirect from the old URL. Formerly a sibling
// of /house-cleaning/real-estate-cleaning/ and /house-cleaning/ndis-cleaning/
// under Home Cleaning's "Specialist cleaning" group.
//
// Built in the same pass as /house-cleaning/real-estate-cleaning/ and sharing its
// structure deliberately, the same call the two commercial leaves made:
// two pages off one menu group that open differently read as two sites.
//
// NO CONTENT BRIEF EXISTS in content-plans/ for this page. But unlike the
// commercial leaves, this one is NOT drafted from nothing — the Brand
// Foundation Document has a full audience section for it (§7 "Audience 2:
// Airbnb and short-stay hosts", plus §3's third differentiator and §5's
// approved headline/CTA sets). Every positioning claim below traces to that
// document, and the places it is quoted are marked. Copy still needs
// sign-off; approved *positioning* is not the same as approved *page copy*.
//
// ✅ UPDATE (September 2026): the supplied copy for §4 and both FAQ blocks
// came without these brackets, so none of the first five is visible on the
// page any more. The list is kept as the record of what was open. Note the
// page still does not SAY how the calendar sync works, who supplies linen, or
// the same-day cut-off; it now simply does not raise them.
//
// Was: BLOCKS LAUNCH — all six are operational facts only TLB holds, and all
// six ship as visible [brackets] per house convention rather than as plausible
// guesses:
//   - HOW the calendar sync actually works. The BFD says TLB "syncs with
//     your booking calendar" and "manages backend scheduling directly
//     around bookings". That is a real differentiator and the page leans on
//     it, but nothing states the mechanism — iCal feed, channel manager, PMS
//     integration, or a person reading the bookings. Naming a specific
//     integration would fabricate a system. Bracketed in §4 and branded FAQ 1.
//   - LINEN. Does TLB supply and launder linen, or turn the host's own? This
//     is the single biggest cost and logistics question in short-stay
//     cleaning and the page cannot answer it. Bracketed in §4 and
//     non-branded FAQ 3.
//   - CONSUMABLES. The BFD promises restocked essentials "such as toilet
//     paper and olive oil". Who buys them, and are they billed on? Bracketed
//     in §4.
//   - SAME-DAY TURNOVER CUT-OFF. The one thing a host rings about. What is
//     the latest checkout TLB can still turn for a same-day check-in, and is
//     there a booking deadline? Bracketed in branded FAQ 2.
//   - PRICING BASIS. Flat rate per turnover or hourly, and is there a
//     minimum? Bracketed in non-branded FAQ 1. A "from $X" that turns out
//     wrong is worse than no number; the ACCC treats from-pricing as a claim.
//   - [insured], inherited from every sibling page. One answer fixes all.
//
// ⚠️ COMPLIANCE READ REQUIRED on non-branded FAQ 5 (short-stay planning
// rules). It describes NSW's short-term rental accommodation framework and
// the Byron Shire day cap. Those rules are live, contested and periodically
// amended, and a host may act on what this page says. It is written without
// dates, precinct lists or a specific commencement on purpose. It needs a
// verification pass and a visible "last reviewed" date before launch, or it
// should come off the page. See that FAQ's own comment.
//
// NOT BUILT, deliberately: hero video, credibility signals, metrics. No
// direction exists for any of them and the deep-cleaning page's precedent is
// that a credibility block filled on an assumption gets removed again.
