// §0 Metadata. ✅ REWRITTEN against the September 2026 copy-rewrite brief
// (workbook row 18, "Airbnb and short-stay turnovers").
//
// TITLE is the workbook's approved line verbatim. The old one split the mapped
// phrase `airbnb cleaning services` (200/mo) with "and Holiday Let", so the
// page carried the head term nowhere at all; this one carries it contiguously
// and picks up `short stay cleaning` in the modifier. 51 characters.
//
// ⚠️ DESCRIPTION IS *NOT* THE WORKBOOK'S APPROVED LINE, and the divergence is
// deliberate and recorded. The approved meta reads:
//
//   "Airbnb cleaning and same-day turnovers with linen, restocking and a photo
//    report after every changeover. Byron to Palm Beach. Talk to us today."
//
// The brief itself raises three change requests against it and asks for a
// ruling. All three are taken here rather than pasted and left live:
//
//   1. "Byron to Palm Beach" is the coastal cherry-picking BFD §2.1 warns
//      against by name. Those are two towns at opposite ends of the footprint,
//      and describing the service area that way silently excludes the entire
//      inland Northern Rivers and every Tweed town between them — §2.1's own
//      example is that naming only Byron and Ballina "quietly tells somebody
//      in Casino, Murwillumbah or Evans Head that they are not the market".
//      The three regions are named instead, as the old meta already did and as
//      the town band in the render now does.
//   2. "A photo report after every changeover" is a service claim this page
//      does not make. §4's sixth block promises TLB tells the host what it
//      found the same day, which is not the same thing. CUT until somebody
//      confirms photos are standard on every turnover — if they are, the block
//      should say so and the meta can have it back.
//   3. The approved line says "Airbnb cleaning" without "services", so it does
//      not actually contain the mapped phrase. Fixed here: the line now opens
//      on `airbnb cleaning services` contiguously.
//
// 140 characters, and it keeps the approved CTA as its final sentence, which is
// what §7's button label is taken from.
const pageMeta = {
  title: 'Airbnb Cleaning Services - Short Stay | TLB Cleaning',
  description:
    'Airbnb cleaning services and same-day turnovers, with linen and restocking. Northern Rivers, Tweed and Southern Gold Coast. Talk to us today.',
  // ⚠️ Placeholder domain, same as every sibling page. Confirm before launch.
  canonical: 'https://tlbcleaning.com.au/airbnb-holiday-home-cleaning/',
};

const business = {
  name: 'TLB Cleaning',
  url: 'https://tlbcleaning.com.au/',
  logo: '',
  telephone: '+61 404 742 065',
  email: 'hello@tlbcleaning.com.au',
  address: {
    streetAddress: '',
    addressLocality: '',
    addressRegion: '',
    postalCode: '',
    addressCountry: 'AU',
  },
  sameAs: [],
  // BOTH STATES, unlike commercial-cleaning and ndis-cleaning which stop at
  // the border. Deliberate: the BFD's own audience section for short-stay
  // hosts names "the Northern Rivers and Southern Gold Coast" explicitly, and
  // twice. So this page uses the full `locationGroups` below rather than
  // `nswLocationGroups`.
  areaServed: 'Northern Rivers and Tweed NSW, and the Southern Gold Coast QLD',
  description: pageMeta.description,
};

// §1 Hero.
//
// ⚠️ SUPERSEDED NOTE, kept because it records a real disagreement. This used
// to read: "The H1 is the BFD's own approved headline for this audience ('Set
// and forget hosting starts here.') and the CTA is its approved CTA for the
// same block ('Let us handle your turnovers') — not the sitewide 'Get an
// instant quote'. A host is buying an arrangement, not a job, and the CTA
// should say so. The kicker carries the focus keyword, which frees the H1 to
// be a promise rather than a keyword."
//
// The September 2026 copy-rewrite brief overrides both halves, on SEO grounds
// rather than voice grounds, and it is right about the H1: the mapped phrase
// was absent from every heading on the page. The headline is demoted, not cut.
//
// It is more arguable about the CTA, and the brief says so itself: "the live
// CTA is better than the approved one... 'Let us handle your turnovers' is BFD
// §6.5's approved language almost word for word, it names the outcome rather
// than the mechanism, and it speaks to §6.2's insight that a host wants to stop
// thinking about turnovers. 'Talk to us today' is generic and could sit on any
// page on any cleaning site." It is changed anyway, because Rule 4 takes the
// CTA from the final sentence of the approved meta — that is the wording the
// searcher was shown in the result — and because §9.5 wants ONE primary CTA
// repeated, which means all four instances move together or none do.
//
// ⚠️ WORKBOOK CHANGE REQUEST: if row 18 is ever reopened, the better line is
// the one that was already here. Put "Let us handle your turnovers" back into
// the approved meta rather than taking it out of the buttons.
//
// quoteCta.href is still the destination, so there is one form to build, not
// two.
//
// A SCENE PHOTO (family A), not a cut-out figure: the shutters, the ocean
// through them, the squared cushions and the restocked bench are what say
// *holiday let*, and none of them survive a cut-out. So `imageFit` is unset
// and takes Placeholder's `cover` default, and `ratio` is 1/1 because the
// source is 1024×1024 — a box matching the file crops nothing. Regenerate
// square if this is ever reshot, or change both together.
//
// ⚠️ GENERATED, NOT PHOTOGRAPHED. A person who does not exist, in the
// IMAGE-GUIDELINES §3 canonical uniform. Honest as generic service imagery
// and not presented as a named team member, which §7 forbids. A real photo
// of a real TLB cleaner in a real Byron holiday let would do more; treat
// this as a good placeholder rather than the finished job.
// ✅ H1 REWRITTEN (copy-rewrite brief §4). The BFD headline is not cut — it
// moves one line down into the new `subheading` slot, which is what that prop
// was added to Hero.astro for. The exact mapped phrase is scored present or
// absent and was absent from both the H1 and the opening paragraph; the
// extension is what this buyer is actually shopping for, per BFD §6.4 ("working
// straight off the booking calendar") and §6.5's approved "We work to your
// booking calendar, not the other way around."
//
// "Set and forget hosting starts here." is BFD §6.2 in five words — a host is
// perfectly capable of organising a cleaner and the value is in not having to.
// It lands one line lower and loses nothing. The stray double space the live
// markup carried between "hosting" and "starts" is gone with the split.
//
// The KICKER stays as it was: with the H1 now carrying the mapped phrase, the
// eyebrow is where "holiday let" stays visible above the fold, which matters
// for `holiday let cleaning` and for the hosts in this region who do not think
// of themselves as running an Airbnb.
//
// INTRO, as supplied (September 2026): the subheading and lead together read as
// one paragraph. The lead's opener now names all three kinds of property
// ("Airbnb, holiday home and short-term rental") rather than repeating the
// mapped phrase, which the H1 still carries contiguously.
const hero = {
  kicker: 'Airbnb and holiday let cleaning',
  headingLines: ['Airbnb cleaning services,', 'timed to your booking calendar'],
  subheading: 'Set and forget hosting starts here.',
  lead:
    `Airbnb, holiday home and short-term rental cleaning timed to your bookings, essentials restocked and the place guest-ready before check-in. Across the Northern Rivers, the Tweed and the Southern Gold Coast. ${theLine.instant}`,
  cta: { label: 'Talk to us today', href: quoteCta.href },
  image: {
    ratio: '1/1',
    label:
      'A cleaner in an aqua polo and dark teal apron setting a vase of fresh flowers on the dining table of a finished, guest-ready coastal holiday apartment, with restocked towels and essentials on the kitchen bench behind her',
